index 69f602d1456431f95254f12cccd7e2dc3e343ead..8e7cc0e77e2a9e003e76ce2893b61149f823a613 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -23,3 +23,12 @@ zeros, failed `test`, `move` from a proper prefix of its path, removing the whol
 Pointers (RFC 6901); `-` is accepted only to append with `add`. Operations are applied in order and the patch
 is atomic: on failure no result is returned. `__proto__` and similar keys are treated as plain members
 and never reach the prototype chain.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396
+section 2) and returns the merged document as a new value. An object patch is merged into the target
+member by member (a non-object target is treated as `{}`); a `null` member removes that member; any other
+patch value, including an array, replaces the target. Neither argument is modified and the result shares
+no structure with them. `__proto__` and similar keys are treated as plain members. Note that a merge patch
+cannot set a member to `null`. Any JSON value is a valid patch, so it never throws.
